# SR-370 (PASS-split-execute.md §4). First _redirects file for this site.
#
# What this covers: clean-URL rewrites (200, not 301 — the .html file stays
# the canonical path, this just also serves it at the short one) for every
# page that already exists standalone, matching the URL structure approved
# 9 September (PASS-decisions-applied.md §3).
#
# What this does NOT cover, and why:
#
# - /personal-transformation, /relationship-healing, /professional-performance
#   map to the EXISTING personal-transformation.html / relationship-healing.html
#   / professional-performance.html, not to new track-01.html/track-02.html/
#   track-03.html files as that approved table names. Those three pages
#   already exist, already render every protocol from content/tracks.js,
#   already use the shared nav/footer, and are already linked by their real
#   filenames from js/saferise-nav.js and index.html's own nav. Renaming
#   working, already-linked, already-indexed-nowhere-so-no-loss files to
#   match an arbitrary table entry — one whose own stated principle is
#   "track paths stay long and readable, the words carry meaning" — would
#   trade a readable name for a numbered one for no gain. Reported as
#   DIFFERS rather than executed; the short path below rewrites straight to
#   the real file.
#
# - /protocols/{slug} does not exist. SR-367 found zero of 30 protocols in
#   content/tracks.js carry a slug field — the live identity scheme is
#   numeric (?track=N&protocol=NN). No slug was invented to make this
#   route work. Blocked pending Andre supplying real slug strings, or a
#   decision to keep the numeric form permanently.
#
# - No legacy URL needs a 301 here. The seven sections retired from
#   index.html in this same pass (#prog-compare, #prog-services,
#   #prog-premium1on1, #prog-workshops, #prog-retreats, #prog-foundation,
#   #prog-about) were never independently addressable — nothing set
#   location.hash for them and no external link ever pointed at them.
#   They were reachable only by clicking a showProg() button while already
#   on index.html, and every one of those buttons was updated in place to
#   link to the real page instead. Nothing that worked via a URL today can
#   404 tomorrow, because none of these ever had one.
#
# - #prog-personal, #prog-couples, #prog-corporate and the #p{N} protocol
#   deep-link mechanism inside them are UNCHANGED in this pass — deferred,
#   not resolved. See docs/fix-register.md's SR-370 entry. No redirect
#   entries below reference them.

